{%- comment -%}
  main-product — the product page. One section, branching on product type.

  Built 31/08/2026, plain wedding rings first. Second pass: reordered to match
  live's buy box after review. The other types are stubbed at the branch.

  NOT PORTED FROM LIVE'S MARKUP. Live's main-product is 162KB of T4S and shares
  its buy box with main-qv; it could not be read whole even if it were worth
  copying. Built from the DATA and from live's rendered page instead.

  ── THE DATA MODEL, which drives every decision here ──────────────────────

  A plain wedding ring is ONE PRODUCT PER combination of metal, profile, width
  and weight. Its variants are RING SIZES ONLY: 70 of them, A to Z+9.5, priced
  in steps as the size goes up — which is why the page states a RANGE at the
  top and a SELECTED price at the point of purchase. Those are two different
  numbers doing two different jobs; live shows both and it is right to.

    options            Ring Size (the only one)
    custom.ring_metal    "14ct Yellow Gold"
    custom.ring_profile  "Concave"
    custom.ring_width    2.0            (number_decimal)
    custom.ring_weight   "Heavy Weight"
    custom.ring_type     ["Plain Wedding Ring"]
    custom.spin_360      a Sirv .spin URL
    filters.band_width   "2mm"          (the string form; see the slug note)

  So SIZE is a variant picker and METAL IS NAVIGATION — choosing a different
  metal means going to a different product.

  ── HOW THE METAL SWITCHER FINDS ITS SIBLINGS ─────────────────────────────

  Handles are perfectly systematic, verified against live 31/08/2026:

      {metal}-{profile}-wedding-ring-{width}-{weight}
      14ct-yellow-gold-concave-wedding-ring-2mm-heavy
      platinum-concave-wedding-ring-25mm-medium

  so the ten metal siblings are CONSTRUCTED and looked up with all_products.
  No app, no metafield list, no JS. Two consequences:

    · `all_products` is capped at TWENTY unique handles per page. Ten metals
      fits; adding profile (9), width (many) or weight (4) switchers the same
      way would blow through it. Do not add another row here.
    · a handle that does not exist returns nothing and that metal renders
      unavailable — a greyed swatch rather than a dead link.

  The width slug is the irregular part: 2.5mm appears in handles as "25mm", so
  it comes from `filters.band_width | remove: '.'`, not from `handle`, which
  would give "2-5mm" and 404.

  ── DIFFERENCES FROM LIVE, deliberate ─────────────────────────────────────

  · SIZE IS A DROPDOWN, not live's grid of 70 chips. Ed's call. The grid was
    four rows of pills that dominated the buy box and pushed the price and the
    button below the fold.
  · A METAL ROW that live does not have. The catalogue splits metal across
    products, so without it the only way to see the same ring in platinum is
    to go back to the collection and filter again.
  · NO SEPARATE SPEC TABLE. The description already lists metal, profile,
    width and band depth as bullets; a table beside it said everything twice.
  · Wishlist is NOT rendered. It is an app feature (settings.wishlist_mode)
    that v3 does not carry yet — a dead heart is worse than no heart.

  ── STILL OPEN ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  custom.spin_360 holds a Sirv 360 spin for every plain band, and live shows it
  as a second thumbnail with a 360 badge. Rendering it needs Sirv's viewer
  script — a third-party script in a theme with one JS file by design — so it
  is not wired up. Hook marked in the gallery. Ed's decision.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign p = product
  assign cf = p.metafields.custom

  assign ring_type = cf.ring_type.value | first | default: p.type
  assign is_plain = false
  if ring_type contains 'Plain Wedding'
    assign is_plain = true
  endif

  assign current = p.selected_or_first_available_variant

  assign profile_slug = cf.ring_profile | handle
  assign width_slug = p.metafields.filters.band_width | remove: '.'
  assign weight_slug = cf.ring_weight | split: ' ' | first | downcase

  assign metal_names = '9ct Yellow Gold,9ct White Gold,9ct Rose Gold,14ct Yellow Gold,14ct White Gold,14ct Rose Gold,18ct Yellow Gold,18ct White Gold,18ct Rose Gold,Platinum' | split: ','
-%}

<section class="band band--white pdp" data-screen-label="Product">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="pdp__top">

      {%- comment -%} ---- Gallery ---- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="pdp__gallery">
        {%- if p.media.size > 0 -%}
          <div class="pdp__stage">
            {{ p.featured_media | image_url: width: 1400 | image_tag:
               loading: 'eager',
               widths: '400,600,900,1200,1400',
               sizes: '(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 55vw',
               alt: p.featured_media.alt | default: p.title,
               class: 'pdp__hero' }}
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            360 SPIN HOOK. Live renders a second thumbnail here carrying a
            "360°" badge, sourced from cf.spin_360 (a Sirv .spin URL). Wiring
            it needs Sirv's viewer script; pending a decision. When added it
            becomes a thumbnail in this list, not a replacement for the stills.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if p.media.size > 1 -%}
            <ul class="pdp__thumbs">
              {%- for media in p.media limit: 8 -%}
                <li>
                  <a class="pdp__thumb" href="{{ media | image_url: width: 1400 }}">
                    {{ media | image_url: width: 220 | image_tag:
                       loading: 'lazy',
                       widths: '110,220',
                       sizes: '96px',
                       alt: '' }}
                  </a>
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- else -%}
          <div class="pdp__stage pdp__stage--empty"></div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} ---- Buy box, in live's order ---- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="pdp__buy">

        <h1 class="pdp__title">{{ p.title }}</h1>

        {%- comment -%}
          The RANGE, not the selected price. On a ring priced by size these are
          different questions — "what do these cost" versus "what does mine
          cost" — and the second one belongs next to the button, below.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="pdp__range">
          {%- if p.price_varies -%}
            Price range: {{ p.price_min | money }} – {{ p.price_max | money }}
          {%- else -%}
            {{ p.price | money }}
          {%- endif -%}
        </p>

        <div class="pdp__meta">
          {%- if current.sku != blank -%}
            <p class="pdp__metarow"><span class="pdp__metakey">SKU</span> <span data-fye-sku>{{ current.sku }}</span></p>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- assign shown = 0 -%}
          {%- if p.collections.size > 0 -%}
            <p class="pdp__metarow">
              <span class="pdp__metakey">Categories</span>
              {%- for c in p.collections -%}
                {%- unless c.handle == 'all' -%}
                  {%- if shown > 0 -%}<span aria-hidden="true">, </span>{%- endif -%}
                  <a href="{{ c.url }}">{{ c.title }}</a>
                  {%- assign shown = shown | plus: 1 -%}
                {%- endunless -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          Live puts the description HERE, above the choices — it is what tells
          you the band depth and the size range before you pick. Kept.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if p.description != blank -%}
          <div class="pdp__desc rte">{{ p.description }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if is_plain and profile_slug != blank and width_slug != blank and weight_slug != blank -%}
          <div class="pdp__field">
            <p class="pdp__label">Metal<span class="pdp__labelval">{{ cf.ring_metal }}</span></p>
            <ul class="pdp__metals">
              {%- for name in metal_names -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign metal_slug = name | handle
                  assign sib_handle = metal_slug | append: '-' | append: profile_slug | append: '-wedding-ring-' | append: width_slug | append: '-' | append: weight_slug
                  assign sib = all_products[sib_handle]
                  assign is_current = false
                  if name == cf.ring_metal
                    assign is_current = true
                  endif
                  assign swatch_token = name | handle | prepend: '--metal-' | replace: '--metal-9ct-', '--metal-9-' | replace: '--metal-14ct-', '--metal-14-' | replace: '--metal-18ct-', '--metal-18-' | replace: '-gold', ''
                -%}
                <li>
                  {%- if is_current -%}
                    <span class="pdp__metal is-current" style="--sw: var({{ swatch_token }});" aria-current="true">
                      <span class="pdp__swatch"></span>
                      <span class="visually-hidden">{{ name }}, selected</span>
                    </span>
                  {%- elsif sib != blank -%}
                    <a class="pdp__metal" href="{{ sib.url }}" style="--sw: var({{ swatch_token }});">
                      <span class="pdp__swatch"></span>
                      <span class="visually-hidden">{{ name }} — from {{ sib.price_min | money }}</span>
                    </a>
                  {%- else -%}
                    <span class="pdp__metal is-off" style="--sw: var({{ swatch_token }});">
                      <span class="pdp__swatch"></span>
                      <span class="visually-hidden">{{ name }}, not made in this profile and width</span>
                    </span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- form 'product', p, class: 'pdp__form', id: 'pdp-form' -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ current.id }}" data-fye-variant-id>

          {%- comment -%}
            The variant JSON the price/SKU updater reads. A data island, not a
            script — same pattern as fye-chapter-nav. Only the three fields the
            buy box actually shows, so it stays small on a 70-variant product.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <script type="application/json" data-fye-variants>
            [
              {%- for v in p.variants -%}
                {"id":{{ v.id }},"title":{{ v.title | json }},"price":{{ v.price | json }},"sku":{{ v.sku | json }},"available":{{ v.available }}}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            ]
          </script>

          {%- if p.has_only_default_variant == false -%}
            {%- for option in p.options_with_values -%}
              <div class="pdp__field">
                <label class="pdp__label" for="pdp-opt-{{ forloop.index }}">
                  {{ option.name }}
                  {%- if option.name == 'Ring Size' and s.size_guide_url != blank -%}
                    <a class="pdp__sizelink" href="{{ s.size_guide_url }}">Find my size</a>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </label>
                <select class="pdp__select"
                        id="pdp-opt-{{ forloop.index }}"
                        name="options[{{ option.name | escape }}]"
                        data-fye-option>
                  {%- for value in option.values -%}
                    <option value="{{ value | escape }}"{% if option.selected_value == value %} selected{% endif %}>{{ value }}</option>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </select>
              </div>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if s.engraving -%}
            <div class="pdp__field">
              <label class="pdp__label" for="pdp-engraving">
                {{ s.engraving_label | default: 'Engraving' }}
                <span class="pdp__labelnote">Optional</span>
              </label>
              <input class="pdp__input"
                     type="text"
                     id="pdp-engraving"
                     name="properties[{{ s.engraving_label | default: 'Engraving' | escape }}]"
                     maxlength="{{ s.engraving_max | default: 30 }}"
                     placeholder="{{ s.engraving_placeholder | escape }}">
              {%- if s.engraving_hint != blank -%}
                <p class="pdp__hint fine">{{ s.engraving_hint }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          <p class="pdp__selected">
            <span class="pdp__selectedkey">Selected price</span>
            <span class="pdp__selectedval" data-fye-price>{{ current.price | money }}</span>
          </p>

          <button class="btn btn--block pdp__atc" type="submit" name="add" data-fye-atc{% unless current.available %} disabled{% endunless %}>
            {%- if current.available -%}
              {{ s.atc_label | default: 'Add to bag' }}
            {%- else -%}
              Made to order — enquire
            {%- endif -%}
          </button>
        {%- endform -%}

        {%- if s.enquire_label != blank -%}
          <a class="btn btn--outline btn--block pdp__enquire" href="{{ s.enquire_link | default: '/pages/contact-us' }}">{{ s.enquire_label }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if s.reassurance != blank -%}
          <p class="pdp__reassure fine">{{ s.reassurance }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
.fye .pdp__top {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr;
  gap: var(--s10);
  align-items: start;
}

/* --- gallery ------------------------------------------------------------- */

.fye .pdp__stage {
  background: var(--ivory);
}

.fye .pdp__hero {
  width: 100%;
  aspect-ratio: 1;
  object-fit: cover;
}

.fye .pdp__stage--empty {
  aspect-ratio: 1;
}

.fye .pdp__thumbs {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: var(--s2);
  margin: var(--s2) 0 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.fye .pdp__thumbs > li {
  margin: 0;
}

.fye .pdp__thumb {
  display: block;
  width: 96px;
  background: var(--ivory);
  border: 1px solid transparent;
}

.fye .pdp__thumb:hover {
  border-color: var(--sage);
}

/* --- buy box ------------------------------------------------------------- */

.fye .pdp__buy {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s5);
}

.fye .pdp__title {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-h3);
}

/* The range is orientation, not the transaction — soft, and a step down from
   the selected price beside the button. */
.fye .pdp__range {
  margin: calc(var(--s5) * -1 + var(--s2)) 0 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__meta {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s2);
  padding-bottom: var(--s5);
  border-bottom: var(--hairline);
}

.fye .pdp__metarow {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
}

.fye .pdp__metakey {
  display: inline-block;
  min-width: 88px;
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__desc {
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
}

.fye .pdp__field {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s2);
}

.fye .pdp__label {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--s4);
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

/* The chosen value sits in the label as well as the control, so the selection
   is readable without opening a 70-item list. */
.fye .pdp__labelval,
.fye .pdp__labelnote,
.fye .pdp__sizelink {
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  font-weight: var(--fw-light);
  letter-spacing: 0;
  text-transform: none;
}

.fye .pdp__labelval {
  color: var(--ink);
}

.fye .pdp__labelnote {
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__sizelink {
  border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;
}

/* --- metal swatches ------------------------------------------------------ */

.fye .pdp__metals {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: var(--s2);
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.fye .pdp__metals > li {
  margin: 0;
}

.fye .pdp__metal {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  width: 44px;
  height: 44px;
  border: 1px solid transparent;
}

.fye .pdp__swatch {
  display: block;
  width: 28px;
  height: 28px;
  background: var(--sw);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--gem-edge);
}

.fye .pdp__metal:hover {
  border-color: var(--sage);
}

.fye .pdp__metal.is-current {
  border-color: var(--line-strong);
}

/* Not made in this profile and width. Shown rather than hidden, so the row
   always states the full range. */
.fye .pdp__metal.is-off {
  opacity: 0.35;
  cursor: not-allowed;
}

/* --- form ---------------------------------------------------------------- */

.fye .pdp__form {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s5);
  margin: 0;
}

.fye .pdp__select,
.fye .pdp__input {
  width: 100%;
}

.fye .pdp__hint {
  margin: 0;
}

/* The number that answers "what does MINE cost", sat directly above the
   button. Full strength and larger than the range at the top. */
.fye .pdp__selected {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--s4);
  margin: 0;
  padding-top: var(--s5);
  border-top: var(--hairline);
}

.fye .pdp__selectedkey {
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__selectedval {
  font-size: var(--fs-h4);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
}

.fye .pdp__reassure {
  margin: 0;
}

/* --- breakpoints. Media queries LAST, always. ---------------------------- */

@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .fye .pdp__top {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--s7);
  }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Main product",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "fye-main-product",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Buy box" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "atc_label", "label": "Add to bag label", "default": "Add to bag" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "size_guide_url", "label": "Ring size guide" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "enquire_label", "label": "Secondary button label", "default": "Contact us about this ring" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "enquire_link", "label": "Secondary button link" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "reassurance",
      "label": "Reassurance line",
      "default": "Handmade to order in the UK. Free delivery, complimentary resizing for a year."
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Engraving" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "engraving", "label": "Offer engraving", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "engraving_label", "label": "Field label", "default": "Engraving" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "engraving_placeholder", "label": "Placeholder", "default": "A date, a name, a few words" },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "engraving_max",
      "label": "Maximum characters",
      "min": 10,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "ch",
      "default": 30
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "engraving_hint",
      "label": "Helper text",
      "default": "Engraved inside the band. Free of charge, and it does not affect delivery time."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Main product" }]
}
{% endschema %}
